Potential problem: parent groups that become empty remain (fine). Also some group may have scale transforms; matrixWorld applies correctly.

Another problem: merged geometry normals when applying non-uniform scale — applyMatrix4 on geometry transforms normals using normal matrix automatically? BufferGeometry.applyMatrix4 uses Matrix3.getNormalMatrix and transforms normals. Yes.

Potential issue: geometries with `uv1`, `color`, `tangent` etc. We delete extras; fine. But `toNonIndexed()` returns with same attributes. Good.

Potential issue: material maps with different UV scaling (building facades) are baked in geometry, fine.

Potential issue: `MeshBasicMaterial` signs with map and transparent false, merged. They are planes; culling okay. But `side` may be FrontSide; merged inherits material side. Fine.

Potential issue: merging geometry groups from different objects with the same material but different renderOrder or polygonOffset (road markings may use polygonOffset). If same material shares, fine. But roads are each separate mesh with same geometry/material and road meshes are used for something? `this.roadMeshes` is array. If merged and removed, `roadMeshes` references detached meshes. Is roadMeshes used? grep.

